// Combined Enable AND Trigger Control Summary
// ========================================================================
// This subsystem uses BOTH enable and trigger control mechanisms:
//
// Enable Control:
//   - Enable signal > 0: Subsystem is allowed to execute
//   - Enable signal <= 0: Subsystem is disabled
//
// Trigger Control:
//   - Trigger event detected: Subsystem can execute (if also enabled)
//   - No trigger event: Subsystem does not execute
//
// Combined Logic:
//   - Execution requires: isEnabled() AND isTriggered()
